# 3-arg case: zero-arg constructor pattern matches a payload-bearing variant.
# [Result.Ok] with zero args in the pattern should tag-check only (no payload.is_none() check).
# This is the "tag-only check" form used with [let _] wildcard or when the payload
# is accessed separately via [let v] binding of the whole scrutinee.
[match [Ok 42]
  [case [let _] [Result.Ok]    "ok"]
  [case [let _] [Result.Error] "error"]
  [case [let _] _              "other"]]
=== out
String("ok")

=== warn
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: Ok
